## Parser-Hinweise Batch 20

```
# ===== XRISM DARTS API JSON-Format ========================================
# DARTS JAXA API:
# {
#   "observations": [
#     {
#       "obsid": "100005010",
#       "target": "Perseus Cluster",
#       "ra": 49.95,
#       "dec": 41.52,
#       "exposure_ks": 210.5,
#       "start_time": "2024-01-25T10:23:00Z",
#       "instrument": "Resolve+Xtend"
#     }, ...
#   ]
# }
# Resolve Energieauflösung: ~7 eV FWHM bei 6 keV
# → Fe XXV He-α triplet (6.70 keV) auflösbar von Fe XXVI Ly-α (6.97 keV)
# ⚠ XRISM DR1 enthält ~10 Zielquellen; wächst kontinuierlich
# velocity_fe: Doppler-Verschiebung des Fe-XXV-Linienkomplexes (km/s)

# ===== ANTARES/Lasair Alert Broker Format ================================
# ANTARES gibt strukturierte JSON-Objekte zurück:
# {
#   "locus_id": "ANT25_abc123",
#   "ra_deg": 180.456,
#   "dec_deg": -23.45,
#   "created": "2026-07-27T00:15:32Z",
#   "num_alerts": 12,
#   "properties": {
#     "ztf_object_id": "ZTF26aabc",
#     "mag_latest": 19.4,
#     "filter_latest": "r"
#   },
#   "tags": ["nuclear_transient", "likely_AGN"]
# }
# tags: ML-Klassifizierung
# Rubin LSST Alert Format (AVRO): komplexer als ZTF; höhere Datendichte
# ⚠ Beide Broker in aktiver Entwicklung für LSST; API kann sich ändern

# ===== GFED5 API Format ===================================================
# GFED5 gibt JSON zurück mit verbrannten Flächenzellen:
# {
#   "grid_cells": [
#     {
#       "lat_center": -15.125,
#       "lon_center": -55.875,
#       "burned_area_ha": 12450.3,
#       "burned_fraction": 0.12,
#       "month": 8,
#       "year": 2024,
#       "dominant_biome": "tropical_forest"
#     }, ...
#   ]
# }
# dominant_biome Codes:
#   tropical_forest, temperate_forest, boreal_forest, savanna,
#   grassland, shrubland, agricultural, peatland
# ⚠ 0.25° × 0.25° Gitter; burned_ha = burned_fraction × cell_area_ha

# ===== COS-Halos VizieR Format ============================================
# Ion-Codes im COS-Halos Katalog:
#   OVI = Sauerstoff VI (O5+); 1031.9 + 1037.6 Å FUV
#   CIV = Kohlenstoff IV (C3+); 1548.2 + 1550.8 Å UV
#   MgII = Magnesium II (Mg+); 2796.4 + 2803.5 Å NUV
#   HI = Lyman-α; 1215.7 Å FUV (Wasserstoff)
# EW: Äquivalentbreite in Å (Rest-Frame); > 50 mÅ = starke Absorption
# logNHI: log10(N/cm⁻²); > 20.3 = DLA, 19-20.3 = sub-DLA
# Metal: [X/H] relativ zu Sonne (dex); < -1.5 = niedrige Metallizität

# ===== e-CALLISTO Solar Radio Burst Format ================================
# e-CALLISTO Event JSON:
# {
#   "event_id": "ECALL_2026_07_27_143512",
#   "start_time": "2026-07-27T14:35:12Z",
#   "end_time": "2026-07-27T14:47:33Z",
#   "type": "III",
#   "frequency_start": 450,   # MHz (Type III: high → low)
#   "frequency_end": 80,      # MHz
#   "peak_flux": 45.3,        # sfu (Solar Flux Units)
#   "station": {"name": "Bleien", "latitude": 47.3, "longitude": 8.2}
# }
# Type II: 0.1-2 MHz/min Drift → Schock (CME-getrieben)
# Type III: 100-1000 MHz/s Drift → Elektronen-Bündel
# Type IV: kontinuierlich → langanhaltende Emission nach Flare

# ===== ACT DR5 Cluster / tSZ Catalog Format ==============================
# Y500: SZ-Signal; Y = integral of y-parameter over solid angle (arcmin²)
# Y500 ∝ M_gas × T → Proxy für Clustermasse M500
# M500: Masse innerhalb R500 (Radius, wo Dichte = 500 × Ρ_crit)
# Typische Werte: M500 ~ 1-10 × 10^14 M_Sun
# ⚠ Cluster bei z > 0.5: starke photo-z-Unsicherheit → Spektroskopie nötig
```

